  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lubia polo is the kind of dish that makes a house smell extraordinary. Lamb simmers low and slow with tomato and spice until it is very tender. Green beans go in towards the end. The whole filling is then layered with parboiled basmati and steamed together for forty minutes, the rice slowly absorbing the perfume of everything beneath it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The tahdig here is particularly good. Lamb juices seep into the base as it steams. The crust picks up a depth that plain potato or bread tahdig never has."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use lamb shoulder or neck fillet; both give more flavour than leg for this kind of slow cooking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
